    {
      "version": "0.2.1",
      "date": "2026-11-02",
      "notes": "Faster, steadier Agent chats. Past chats appear at once: the list is read from Codex's own chat index in a few milliseconds instead of asking Codex to scan every saved session (4-10 seconds on a long history), and it is kept between launches. Opening a chat is instant: each turn's message and answer show first, then what Codex did in the latest turn; older turns have a \"Show what Codex did\" row that loads on click. Large chats (Unity screenshots in tool results) no longer drop the Codex connection. Every chat request has a time limit and says what went wrong in the chat, picking chats quickly always shows the last one picked, chats keep their history after Codex stops unexpectedly, and a chat open in another Codex window (VS Code) says so. The bundled Unity Tools packages are unchanged (Base 0.1.6, Play 0.1.11, Edit 0.6.23, Debug 0.1.4).",
