      "notes": "A new look for every screen. The tools work exactly as before; only how they look and where a few controls sit changed. The window has a full-height sidebar and one toolbar with the project, the tool tabs (Overview, Play, Agent, Edit, Debug, each with its own colour), Unity's state and Open in Unity. Press ⌘K (Ctrl+K) to jump to any project or tool or run a command. Overview shows Unity's state, script errors and a tile per tool. Play's Play/Pause/Step sit in the middle like Unity's toolbar. Agent has a calmer reading column, a timeline of tool calls, clearer approval cards and suggestions on an empty chat. Edit's designer panel is grouped into cards. Debug's script editor has line numbers and C# colours, and New Session opens a small dialog. Settings has a section list and theme previews. New icons, menus, dialogs, notifications and app icon; refined light and dark themes. The bundled Unity Tools packages are unchanged (Base 0.1.6, Play 0.1.11, Edit 0.6.23, Debug 0.1.4).",
